{
  "question": "needs_judgment (agent.yml Gate, typed choice judgment|mechanical): which MiniMax variant answers the Gate best on the shipped held-out cases",
  "cases_file": "tests/evals/cases/needs_judgment.json",
  "source": "tests/evals/cases/needs_judgment.json (unchanged): 60 0509 issues labelled agent-ready, labelled by the judge group (openai/qwen3.8-max, a non-Claude family), split test",
  "split_use": "this decision spends the split: choosing between the two MiniMax variants on these 60 cases means they are no longer a clean held-out set for a later change to either MiniMax row. A later change to those rows needs cases written and labelled after 2026-10-20.",
  "decision": "no router weight for the added id. The provider list grew one id on 2026-10-20; the probe answered, and on the Gate's own held-out cases it routed 47/60 against 50/60 for the id already in rotation, so it takes no row: it scores below the row it would join (issue #9915's acceptance (c): \"a model that scores lower than the one it replaces gets no extra weight\"), and a row for it would in any case need Nish's yes first, because the approved-models list at the top of config/litellm-proxy.yaml names MiniMax: M3.1-Flash-Preview only (2026-09-28). No row and no setting in config/litellm-proxy.yaml changes: the four MiniMax rows are exactly as they were, and the only change to that file is a comment recording these numbers.",
  "case_record": "tests/evals/cases/needs_judgment.json is the case set and is unchanged by this PR. The rows scored here are held once, in this file, so nothing can drift between two copies; a worker that enumerates tests/evals/cases/ finds case sets only.",
  "labeller": {
    "group": "judge",
    "served_model": "openai/qwen3.8-max",
    "router_row": "alibaba-qwen38max-judge",
    "calls": 0,
    "note": "no new labels: the builder scored the already-labelled cases, so the family that wrote the labels neither wrote nor graded anything here. The builder is Claude; the labels and the held-out split predate it. The builder ran the score, but it graded a MiniMax family's answers against labels a third family wrote: no Claude output is graded and no Claude labels are read as ground truth for it"
  },
  "scorer": {
    "endpoint": "POST https://api.minimax.io/anthropic/v1/messages (the provider's own anthropic-compatible path, key from the seat file through a 0600 header file, never argv)",
    "served_model": [
      "MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview (the id the router serves today; sent bare on the direct call, the anthropic/ prefix on the router rows is LiteLLM notation)",
      "MiniMax-M3.1-Flash (the id the provider list added 2026-10-20, sent bare on the direct call)"
    ],
    "calls": "120 scored (60 cases x 2 variants, one read each); the discarded 256-token pass was another 120 on the same flat plan",
    "repeats": 1,
    "request": "the Gate's own question and choice criteria from agent.yml's judgment_p, verbatim, over title + the first 6000 chars of body",
    "reading": "choice and probability parsed from the reply text; a case with no JSON gets no band and is counted as middle (the free lane), the way a Jev error routes"
  },
  "tuning": "none on either side: the question, the criteria and the case labels are the shipped ones, and neither variant's prompt was tuned. max_tokens was raised from 256 to 1024 after a first pass because both variants emit a thinking block first and 256 truncated it before any JSON text arrived; that was a harness artefact on both sides, so both variants were rescored at the same value. The discarded 256-token pass cost another 120 reads on the same flat plan and is disclosed here rather than dropped.",
  "bands": {
    "claude": "p(judgment) >= 0.9",
    "free": "p(judgment) <= 0.1",
    "middle": "otherwise (routes to the free lanes)"
  },
